/-
# Dregg2.Tools.ConeCutoverListCommit — the CUTOVER of the `ListDigestBindsList` cluster: the first
REALIZED surface reduction of the vacuity-elimination campaign.

The 13 threaders `Tools/ConePort` verified portable (kernel-checked S3 successors, committed as
`Circuit/ListCommitPortedCone`) are cut over IN PLACE: each original keeps its NAME and its
CONCLUSION but loses the refuted `compressNInjective` (`+ listLeafInjective`) floor binder for the
per-instance `¬ CNColl`/`¬ ListColl` side condition — the exact type the cone port pinned
(re-verified by `Circuit/ListCommitCutoverCheck`'s `example : ⟨cone type⟩ := @original` teeth).
Consumers still carrying their own floor binder discharge the side condition through the
`ListCommitRegrounded.noCNColl_of_inj` / `noColl_of_carriers` bridges — which makes the NEXT cone
level uniformly portable (the bridge `AppRule` in `Tools/ConePortListCommitRun.bridgeRules` closes
the level-2 composition gap). The additive scaffolding module `Circuit/ListCommitPortedCone.lean`
is RETIRED in the same transaction: a port that leaves the vacuous original standing reduces the
surface by zero, and so does a cutover that leaves the duplicate port standing.

In DEFAULT mode (every build) this module is the standing textual tooth that the cutover HOLDS:
every pre-cutover fragment absent, every cutover fragment present, the retired file gone. The
semantic teeth live beside it: `ListCommitCutoverCheck` (statement identity to the ConePort-pinned
types + floor unreachability) and the re-pinned `ConePortListCommitRun` driver (the 13 now REFUSE
as not-a-carrier — the floor binders are measurably gone).

One-shot application: `scripts/cone_cutover_run.sh` (backups → `CONE_CUTOVER_WRITE=1` staged
transaction → closure build → ruler; rollback on any red).
-/
